<title>MEXICO: Mexico Sept silver output up, other metals mixed.</title>
<headline>Mexico Sept silver output up, other metals mixed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico, the world's largest silver producer, saw September silver output rise slightly to 203,419 kg from the 201,803 kg produced in the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said silver output in the first nine months of the year dipped 0.4 percent from the same period in 1995.</p>
<p>A breakdown of metals and minerals production in the first nine months follows.  </p>
<p>    Product    Sept 96    Sept 95     Jan-Sept  Pct Chge Vs 95</p>
<p>    Gold	   1,692	1,532	16,728	  18.1</p>
<p>    Silver     203,419    201,803   1,854,396	  -0.4</p>
<p>    Lead	  13,147     11,327     120,921	 -10.8</p>
<p>    Copper	25,225     28,440     245,968	  -1.1</p>
<p>    Zinc	  28,168     29,439     255,987	  -1.0</p>
<p>    Coal	 825,186    655,698   6,516,276	  26.6</p>
<p>    Iron	 583,757    427,560   4,622,220	  14.8</p>
<p>    Sulphur     70,750     77,536     699,826	   4.7</p>
<p>    Dolomite    74,610     70,782     765,248	   N/A</p>
<p>    Gypsum     361,601    365,819   2,719,814	   2.7</p>
<p>    Phosphorite 51,140     51,757     516,465	   N/A</p>
<p>Legend: Precious metals output in kilos, others in tonnes. Coal output in mineral volume. Figures revised from January-August figures given by INEGI.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530</p>
